{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Household Survey Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "Coverage, enumerator performance, and submission trends",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Households Surveyed",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Unique Villages Covered",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"village\") AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Active Enumerators",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"enumerator_name\") AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Submissions by Village",
    "sql": "SELECT \"village\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"household_survey\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 20",
    "x": "village",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Submissions by Enumerator",
    "sql": "SELECT \"enumerator_name\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"household_survey\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "enumerator_name",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Daily Submission Trend",
    "sql": "SELECT DATE(\"_submission_time\") AS date, COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"household_survey\" WHERE \"_submission_time\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "date",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard provides a high-level overview of the household survey operations. A total of {{p1}} households have been surveyed across {{p2}} unique villages. The data collection effort was supported by {{p3}} active enumerators.\n\nThe distribution of surveys across villages varies, with the bar chart highlighting the top 20 villages by volume. Similarly, the enumerator performance chart shows the workload distribution among the field team.\n\nFinally, the trend line tracks the daily submission volume over time, allowing for the identification of peak collection periods and potential gaps in data entry."
 },
